62	 * {@link Endpoint}s using {@link EndpointWeightTransition},
63	 * {@code rampingUpIntervalMillis} and {@code rampingUpTaskWindow}.
64	 * If more than one {@link Endpoint} are added within the {@code rampingUpTaskWindow}, the weights of
65	 * them are updated together. If there's already a scheduled job and new {@link Endpoint}s are added
66	 * within the {@code rampingUpTaskWindow}, they are updated together.
67	 * This is an example of how it works when {@code rampingUpTaskWindow} is 500 milliseconds and
68	 * {@code rampingUpIntervalMillis} is 2000 milliseconds:
69	 * <pre>{@code
70	 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
71	 *     A         B                             C                                       D
72	 *     t0        t1                            t2                                      t3         t4
73	 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
74	 *     0ms       t0 + 200ms                    t0 + 1000ms                          t0 + 1800ms  t0 + 2000ms
75	 * }</pre>
76	 * A and B are ramped up right away when they are added and they are ramped up together at t4.
77	 * C is updated alone every 2000 milliseconds. D is ramped up together with A and B at t4.
78	 */
